{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>המן</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others המן הסלע הזה, המן הגורן או מן היקב. Like the one who says: the tree from which the first man ate was wheat, and this is המן הגורן; and just as death was decreed upon him because of המן העץ, so too there death was decreed through המן הסלע." "<b>אשר צויתיך לבלתי אכל</b> ס\"ת רכיל — you walked in the counsel of a talebearer."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The word המן here means 'from it/the tree' (הִמֵּן = הַמִּן, 'from it'); the juxtaposition plays on the identical spelling with other phrases where המן = 'the man' (Haman)."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:36.352378816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}